# Advice for shipping-work's doc-check.sh (Step 1.5): the doc sections to
# spot-check when an entry in .skills/doc-sensitive-paths hits (GH #210).
#
# Grammar: one line per section; blank lines and whole-line #-comments
# ignored; each line printed verbatim as a bullet. This file REPLACES the
# skill's two built-in lines, which describe a layout this repo does not keep
# (e.g. they send a routers/ hit to an AGENTS.md "route table" that does not
# exist — README.md "Endpoints" and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md hold it here).
#
# Line shape, which the drift test depends on:
#   <one tracked doc>: "<heading>", "<heading>" — what drifts (entries that route here)
# Quotes are reserved for heading names. Verify after any doc rename or
# heading edit with:
#   uv run pytest tests/unit/test_doc_sections.py
#
# Kept in step with doc-sensitive-paths by the same test: every entry there is
# a line's doc or named as a whole token in some line's parenthetical — an
# entry named nowhere gets advice about everything but itself on a hit.
# Upstream checks nothing about advice (gregoryfoster/skills#284). One entry is
# exempt (_UNROUTED in the test): .github/workflows/ — no doc inventories it;
# its one workflow (context-cadence.yml) documents itself.

# --- Policy file + README: contract, auth, commands, ops, agent plumbing ---
